{"abstract":"The idea of pushing computation to storage devices has been explored for decades, without widespread adoption so far. The definition of Computational Programs namespaces in NVMe (TP 4091) might be a breakthrough. The proposal defines device-specific programs, that are installed statically, and downloadable programs, offloaded from a host at run-time using eBPF. In this paper, we present the design and implementation of Delilah, the first public description of an actual computational storage device supporting eBPF-based code offload. We conduct experiments to evaluate the overhead of eBPF function execution in Delilah, and to explore design options. This study constitutes a baseline for future work.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hedam, Niclas","Clausen, Morten Tychsen","Bonnet, Philippe","Lee, Sangin","Larsen, Ken Friis"],"cuid":["S02-083.04-692213"],"event":{"end":"2023-06-23","place":"Seattle, us","start":"2023-06-18","title":"19th International Workshop on Data Management on New Hardware, DaMoN 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Fribourg"],"keyword":["Code offloading","Computational storage","NVMe namespaces","Storage device performance","eBPF"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"delilah ebpf offload on computational storage","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3592980.3595319","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-083.04-692213","identifier":[{"id":"85163736061","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d6484671-b01d-4954-a04e-f594e27403fe","ku-a42e4598-ec5e-40a6-a009-a2b9cfb47a2e"],"keyword":["Code offloading","Computational storage","NVMe namespaces","Storage device performance","eBPF"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E659C89D4673EE6796787AA6985BA54B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/98502207/damon23_20.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/360398899/Delilah.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3592980.3595319","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"university of fribourg","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Fribourg","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Programming Languages and Theory of Computation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niclas","key":"hedampau","last":"Hedam","locid":"c07af2ac-7d8d-482a-ba4c-cd9559612df6","name":"Hedam, Niclas","orcid":"0000-0001-5847-8419","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Tychsen","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","locid":"09813918-f2fa-46c2-a9b1-069b140c2903","name":"Clausen, Morten Tychsen","orcid":"0000-0001-8609-0745","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Philippe","key":"bonnetpau","last":"Bonnet","locid":"19e8d8f1-16b3-457d-b02b-89d9ce850c30","name":"Bonnet, Philippe","orcid":"0000-0002-0234-5374","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sangin","key":"leepau","last":"Lee","name":"Lee, Sangin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Ken Friis","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9156682b-05d0-4d40-be10-0d14bafe4d74","name":"Larsen, Ken Friis","orcid":"0000-0002-0990-5127","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3592980.3595319","eisbn":["9781450395076"],"pages":"70-76","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery, Inc.","series":"Proceedings of the 19th International Workshop on Data Management on New Hardware, DaMoN","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 19th International Workshop on Data Management on New Hardware, DaMoN 2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85163736061"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d6484671-b01d-4954-a04e-f594e27403fe","ku-a42e4598-ec5e-40a6-a009-a2b9cfb47a2e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Delilah : eBPF-offload on Computational Storage","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-083.04-692213","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Danish insurance and pension companies are required by financial regulations to report certain financial quantities to prove that they are solvent and managed responsibly. Parts of these quantities are computed the same way for all companies, whereas so-called management actions, describing, e.g., surplus sharing, vary between companies. Hence it is desirable to have a flexible calculation platform that allows actuaries to easily create company-specific models, which are also computationally efficient. In this paper, we present our work with implementing a code generator for a DSL called the Management Action Language (MAL) as a form of variability management. While one of the goals of MAL is to generate efficient code from an actuary’s specification, it is non-trivial how to produce such code. We identify four reoccurring patterns in the models created by actuaries as subjects to optimisations. We describe our process for implementing a code-generator by a) identifying four specification patterns (inheritance, union types, type filtering, and numerical maps) that are pervasive in these calculations, and b) describing how to generate efficient C# from MAL for these patterns. We evaluate the code-generator by benchmarking it against handwritten production code and show an approximate 1.3× speedup in a production environment. This evaluation demonstrates that, with MAL, an individual pension company may reuse the general calculation platform and all of the optimisations built into MAL’s code generator when modelling the company’s business rules.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Borum, Holger Stadel","Clausen, Morten Tychsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383530"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Benchmarking","C optimization","Code generation","Computational efficiency","Domain Specific Language DSL","Management Actions","actuarial modeling","financial regulations","solvency reporting","specification patterns"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transforming domain models to efficient c for the danish pension industry","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3550356.3561580","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383530","identifier":[{"id":"85142924075","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9af92d3c-5907-4d8e-bc32-350209cce937"],"keyword":["C# optimization","Domain-Specific Language (DSL)","actuarial modeling","benchmarking","code generation","computational efficiency","financial regulations","management actions","solvency reporting","specification patterns"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-5108325CD29F8FD62459CC2F8B78C07D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3550356.3561580","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/90366507/holger_morten_MAL.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Holger Stadel","key":"borumpau","last":"Borum","name":"Borum, Holger Stadel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Tychsen","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","locid":"09813918-f2fa-46c2-a9b1-069b140c2903","name":"Clausen, Morten Tychsen","orcid":"0000-0001-8609-0745","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3550356.3561580","status":"p","title":"ACM/IEEE 25th International Conference on Model Driven Engineering Languages and Systems: Companion Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85142924075"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9af92d3c-5907-4d8e-bc32-350209cce937"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Transforming Domain Models to Efficient C# for the Danish Pension Industry","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383530","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
